From f539daa3ac8f6732fbe7f491e93da31e0f604178 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:29:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): deploy parks honour the host core update window
 [daveey]

A deploy wait parked before the host's core update batch opened re-parked on
every wake and its third park escalated to an unstick owner card although the
deploy was only queued. Parks now read <root>/cache/core-update/window.json
(schema v1, fresh <=1200s, never future, this host as hermes-sync's HOST,
well typed). With valid evidence the wake is floored to window_at +
drain_bound_s and the reason names the window in Pacific time. The park is
healthy (neither counted by prior_same_premise nor escalated) only while the
batch is batching/draining and the window is ahead or its semantic state moved
since the previous same-premise park; a newer observed_at alone is not
progress. Missing, stale, foreign or malformed evidence changes nothing.
Wired into schedule_task, timed-park block_task and continue_task before
persistence; wake probes and other gates are unchanged.
---
